### Pattern Variations

**Variation 1: Simplified Error Response (Internal APIs)**

For internal microservice-to-microservice communication where full RFC 7807 overhead not needed:

```json
{
  "type": "validation/required-field",
  "title": "Required Field Missing",
  "status": 400,
  "detail": "memberId is required",
  "correlationId": "7f8d9c2a..."
}
```

Omits: `instance`, `timestamp`, `documentationUrl`, `suggestedAction`

**Variation 2: Batch Operation Errors**

When processing batch of items with partial failures:

```json
{
  "type": "https://api.gainwell.com/errors/batch/partial-failure",
  "title": "Batch Processing Completed with Errors",
  "status": 207,
  "detail": "Processed 100 claims: 95 succeeded, 5 failed",
  "instance": "/api/v1/claims/batch/batch-001",
  "timestamp": "2026-01-15T15:00:00Z",
  "correlationId": "9b8c7a6d...",
  "summary": {
    "total": 100,
    "succeeded": 95,
    "failed": 5
  },
  "failures": [
    {
      "itemId": "claim-003",
      "type": "validation/invalid-format",
      "detail": "Invalid service date format"
    },
    {
      "itemId": "claim-027",
      "type": "business-rule/eligibility-not-met",
      "detail": "Member not eligible on service date"
    }
  ]
}
```

Uses HTTP 207 Multi-Status with error details per failed item.

**Variation 3: FHIR OperationOutcome Alignment**

For FHIR APIs, use OperationOutcome but align structure:

```json
{
  "resourceType": "OperationOutcome",
  "issue": [
    {
      "severity": "error",
      "code": "required",
      "details": {
        "coding": [{
          "system": "https://api.gainwell.com/errors",
          "code": "validation/required-field-missing"
        }],
        "text": "Required Field Missing"
      },
      "diagnostics": "The 'patient' field is required",
      "expression": ["Patient"]
    }
  ],
  "extension": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.gainwell.com/fhir/correlationId",
      "valueString": "7f8d9c2a..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Maintains FHIR compliance while providing consistent error tracking.

