### Before/After Comparison

**Before: Inconsistent Error Handling**

**Scenario**: Provider checks eligibility, receives inconsistent errors from different APIs

**Claims API Error (Custom Format)**:

```json
{
  "errorCode": "VAL_001",
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "timestamp": "2025-01-15T10:30:00Z"
}
```

**Eligibility API Error (Different Custom Format)**:

```json
{
  "error": {
    "type": "ValidationError",
    "statusCode": 400,
    "message": "Request validation failed",
    "details": ["Member ID is required"]
  }
}
```

**Provider API Error (Minimal Format)**:

```json
{
  "error": "Invalid provider ID"
}
```

**Problems**:

- ❌ Consumer must implement 3 different error parsers
- ❌ No correlation IDs for troubleshooting
- ❌ Vague error messages without actionable guidance
- ❌ No links to documentation
- ❌ Inconsistent field names (errorCode vs error.type vs error)
- ❌ No suggested remediation actions
- ❌ Cannot build generic error handling middleware

**Integration Code Complexity**:

```javascript
// Before: Consumer must handle each API differently
async function callGainwellAPIs() {
  // Claims API error handling
  try {
    await claimsAPI.submit(claim);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.response.data.errorCode) {
      // Custom Claims API format
      logError(error.response.data.errorCode, error.response.data.message);
    }
  }

  // Eligibility API error handling
  try {
    await eligibilityAPI.verify(memberId);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.response.data.error) {
      // Different custom format
      logError(error.response.data.error.type, error.response.data.error.message);
      if (error.response.data.error.details) {
        // Handle details array
      }
    }
  }

  // Provider API error handling
  try {
    await providerAPI.lookup(providerId);
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.response.data.error) {
      // Minimal format - just a string
      logError("UNKNOWN", error.response.data.error);
    }
  }
}
```

**After: RFC 7807 Standard Error Handling**

**All APIs Use Consistent Format**:

```json
{
  "type": "https://api.gainwell.com/errors/validation/required-field-missing",
  "title": "Required Field Missing",
  "status": 400,
  "detail": "The 'memberId' field is required for eligibility verification",
  "instance": "/api/v1/eligibility/verify/req-abc-123",
  "timestamp": "2026-01-15T14:32:10.523Z",
  "correlationId": "7f8d9c2a-4b3e-11ec-81d3-0242ac130003",
  "errors": [
    {
      "field": "memberId",
      "code": "REQUIRED_FIELD",
      "message": "Member ID is required"
    }
  ],
  "suggestedAction": "Provide a valid Member ID in the format XX-XXXXXXX-XX",
  "documentationUrl": "https://api.gainwell.com/docs/errors/validation/required-field-missing"
}
```

**Benefits**:

- ✅ Single error parser works for all Gainwell APIs
- ✅ Correlation IDs enable end-to-end tracing
- ✅ Specific, actionable error messages
- ✅ Documentation links for self-service
- ✅ Consistent field names across all APIs
- ✅ Suggested actions guide consumers to resolution
- ✅ Machine-readable error types enable automation

**Integration Code Simplification**:

```javascript
// After: Generic error handler works for all APIs
async function callGainwellAPIs() {
  try {
    await claimsAPI.submit(claim);
    await eligibilityAPI.verify(memberId);
    await providerAPI.lookup(providerId);
  } catch (error) {
    // Single error handler for all APIs
    handleRFC7807Error(error.response.data);
  }
}

function handleRFC7807Error(problemDetails) {
  // Log with correlation ID
  logger.error({
    errorType: problemDetails.type,
    correlationId: problemDetails.correlationId,
    message: problemDetails.detail
  });

  // Display user-friendly message
  showErrorToUser(problemDetails.title, problemDetails.detail);

  // Show suggested action
  if (problemDetails.suggestedAction) {
    showSuggestion(problemDetails.suggestedAction);
  }

  // Provide documentation link
  if (problemDetails.documentationUrl) {
    showHelpLink(problemDetails.documentationUrl);
  }

  // Handle specific error types programmatically
  if (problemDetails.type.includes('/authentication/expired-token')) {
    await refreshAuthToken();
    // Retry original request
  } else if (problemDetails.type.includes('/rate-limit/')) {
    const retryAfter = problemDetails.retryAfter || 60;
    await sleep(retryAfter * 1000);
    // Retry original request
  }
}
```

**Measured Improvements**:

The standardized error response pattern reduces integration complexity and support burden for API consumers. Teams adopting this pattern benefit from reusable error parsing logic, faster troubleshooting through correlation IDs, and clearer audit trails.
